WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.716
Mrs. Blurrie was very old and lived alone. She liked living by herself.

2
00:00:05.717 --> 00:00:09.982
And though her children begged her to move in with them, she continued to live alone.

3
00:00:09.983 --> 00:00:15.446
One day her independence faced a problem, however, when she noticed that she could not see very well.

4
00:00:15.447 --> 00:00:20.960
She had been making pancakes for breakfast and thought she had added oil to the batter.

5
00:00:20.961 --> 00:00:25.434
However, when she put a bite of pancakes into her mouth, they tasted awful!

6
00:00:25.435 --> 00:00:28.272
She realized she had added soap by mistake!

7
00:00:28.273 --> 00:00:32.846
"I must get my eyes checked," she said to her favorite plant Harry.

8
00:00:32.847 --> 00:00:37.945
So she called Dr. Snatch that afternoon and asked him to come over and examine her eyes.

9
00:00:37.946 --> 00:00:43.621
"I will be there tomorrow morning at nine," the doctor said.

10
00:00:43.622 --> 00:00:49.432
At nine o'clock the doctor arrived. He pulled out his scopes and charts and checked Mrs. Blurrie's vision.

11
00:00:49.433 --> 00:00:54.691
He said "hmm" and "ohh" a lot.

12
00:00:54.692 --> 00:01:00.520
When she looked at his face, Mrs. Blurrie couldn't tell if he was rubbing his head or if it was growing.

13
00:01:00.521 --> 00:01:05.276
Even though Dr. Snatch was sitting close, he looked all blurry.

14
00:01:05.277 --> 00:01:09.330
"I have some bad news, Mrs. Blurrie," he said.

15
00:01:09.331 --> 00:01:15.523
"Your eyes are very old, and you are quickly going blind from a terrible disease."

16
00:01:15.524 --> 00:01:23.756
"Is there nothing you can do to make my eyes better?" Mrs. Blurrie pleaded. "Please, I will do anything!"

17
00:01:23.757 --> 00:01:32.141
"Well, I could do something, but it would be very expensive," Dr. Snatch said.

18
00:01:32.142 --> 00:01:39.056
"Oh, please. I will pay whatever you ask if you will only help me see again," she said.

19
00:01:39.057 --> 00:01:47.501
"Very well," he agreed, "but it will mean that I must come here every day for two weeks to give you a special treatment."

20
00:01:47.502 --> 00:01:51.181
"Agreed. You may come anytime you wish."

21
00:01:51.182 --> 00:01:56.541
Dr. Snatch shook hands with Mrs. Blurrie, and then he left.

22
00:01:56.542 --> 00:02:01.353
For the next two weeks, Dr. Snatch came to Mrs. Blurrie's house every day.

23
00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:07.585
He would begin by having her lie down on the couch for ten minutes with a cloth over her eyes to relax the muscles.

24
00:02:07.586 --> 00:02:11.847
Then he would remove the cloth and place a special lotion on her eyelids.

25
00:02:11.848 --> 00:02:18.469
Finally he would put some drops into her eyes and have her lie down in a dark room for thirty minutes.

26
00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:24.163
When the thirty minutes was over, Mrs. Blurrie would come out of her room, and Dr. Snatch would be gone.

27
00:02:24.164 --> 00:02:28.374
Though Mrs. Blurrie was very patient, she didn't seem to be getting better.

28
00:02:28.375 --> 00:02:33.552
In fact, after every treatment, she couldn't see anything except big shapes and colors.

29
00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:42.265
But every evening she would start to see a little better again, so Mrs. Blurrie told herself the medicine was starting to work.

30
00:02:42.266 --> 00:02:47.047
What Mrs. Blurrie didn't realize was that Dr. Snatch was deceiving her.

31
00:02:47.048 --> 00:02:50.446
He was covering her eyes and having her lie down to trick her.

32
00:02:50.447 --> 00:02:55.047
In fact, the drops that he put in her eyes made her see even worse for a few hours!

33
00:02:55.048 --> 00:02:58.214
Mrs. Blurrie didn't have a terrible eye disease.

34
00:02:58.215 --> 00:03:05.162
Dr. Snatch was making her vision worse so that he could steal from her while she couldn't see!

35
00:03:05.163 --> 00:03:09.396
On the last day Dr. Snatch came to visit, his medicines were different.

36
00:03:09.397 --> 00:03:12.106
He did not ask Mrs. Blurrie to lie down.

37
00:03:12.107 --> 00:03:16.759
He did not put lotion on her eyelids. And he did not put drops in her eyes.

38
00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:22.322
"You are finally ready for the last step, Mrs. Blurrie," he announced proudly.

39
00:03:22.323 --> 00:03:32.808
"I have saved you from an illness that would have made you blind, and now that the disease is gone, we can correct your vision."

40
00:03:32.809 --> 00:03:40.253
With that, Mrs. Blurrie heard the doctor remove something from a paper bag, and then she felt something heavy on her nose and ears.

41
00:03:40.254 --> 00:03:43.250
When she looked straight ahead, she could see perfectly!

42
00:03:43.251 --> 00:03:49.634
Mrs. Blurrie went over to the mirror to see someone she had not seen for a very long time: herself!

43
00:03:49.635 --> 00:03:53.406
In the mirror she saw that she was wearing glasses.

44
00:03:53.407 --> 00:03:59.699
"Why, it's just these glasses that are helping me see," she said, a little disappointed.

45
00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:06.092
"Yes, first we had to cure the disease that was in your eyes so that the glasses could work.

46
00:04:06.093 --> 00:04:12.386
And now you can see!" Dr. Snatch turned to his bag and pulled out a piece of paper.

47
00:04:12.387 --> 00:04:20.263
"Here is my bill for saving your sight," he said, handing her the paper as if he had done something very great.

48
00:04:20.264 --> 00:04:26.195
"My, that must have been very expensive medicine, but we did have an agreement.

49
00:04:26.196 --> 00:04:32.729
Let me go get some money." Mrs. Blurrie turned to go to the kitchen, where she hid her money in the cookie jar.

50
00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:36.015
When she looked at her kitchen, she noticed something strange.

51
00:04:36.016 --> 00:04:42.961
Mrs. Blurrie screamed, "My kitchen is empty! Where are my dishes?

52
00:04:42.962 --> 00:04:48.427
Where are my pictures? Where is my cookie jar?"

53
00:04:48.428 --> 00:04:54.368
All that was left on the counter were the soapy pancakes she had made two weeks ago and Harry, her plant.

54
00:04:54.369 --> 00:04:59.168
When she returned to her living room, she realized that valuables were missing there as well.

55
00:04:59.169 --> 00:05:02.918
"I have been robbed!" Mrs. Blurrie cried.

56
00:05:02.919 --> 00:05:08.490
"I cannot pay you, Dr. Snatch," Mrs. Blurrie said with suspicion.

57
00:05:08.491 --> 00:05:13.357
"I have been robbed, and everything I had that was valuable is gone."

58
00:05:13.358 --> 00:05:19.677
"I am sorry you cannot find what you are looking for, but you must pay me, Mrs. Blurrie.

59
00:05:19.678 --> 00:05:23.126
We had an agreement," he reminded her.

60
00:05:23.127 --> 00:05:27.866
"Yes, but I have nothing with which to pay you," she said.

61
00:05:27.867 --> 00:05:34.500
"Well, then, I will be forced to have the judge put you in prison for failing to pay your bills!"

62
00:05:34.501 --> 00:05:38.527
he said angrily, and he stomped out of the house.

63
00:05:38.528 --> 00:05:44.052
The very next day, Mrs. Blurrie and Dr. Snatch stood before a judge and told their stories.

64
00:05:44.053 --> 00:05:49.009
"Your Honor, this woman agreed to pay me if I helped her see again.

65
00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:54.474
Now that she can see, she tells me she cannot pay," Dr. Snatch said.

66
00:05:54.475 --> 00:05:58.508
"Is that true, Mrs. Blurrie?" the judge asked.

67
00:05:58.509 --> 00:06:06.577
"Yes, Your Honor, it is true. I did agree to pay Dr. Snatch if he helped me see again.

68
00:06:06.578 --> 00:06:15.432
But it is also true that we agreed I would not have to pay him if he did not restore my sight," Mrs. Blurrie replied.

69
00:06:15.433 --> 00:06:19.738
"Well, can you see or not?" the judge asked.

70
00:06:19.739 --> 00:06:28.551
"Sir, Dr. Snatch says I can see. However, I believe that I still cannot," she said.

71
00:06:28.552 --> 00:06:32.687
"Why is that?" asked the judge.

72
00:06:32.688 --> 00:06:44.492
"Your Honor, before I lost my sight I loved to look at all of the valuable things in my home: my silver, my china, my pictures, and my cookie jar.

73
00:06:44.493 --> 00:06:48.761
To this day, I cannot see any of those valuable things.

74
00:06:48.762 --> 00:06:54.920
Thus, I have not been healed, and I don't owe him anything," Mrs. Blurrie insisted.

75
00:06:54.921 --> 00:06:59.753
"I see your point," the judge said as he rubbed his chin.

76
00:06:59.754 --> 00:07:10.059
"Dr. Snatch, since Mrs. Blurrie is unable to see what she once loved to look upon, she has not been cured and owes you nothing.

77
00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:12.468
Thank you and have a nice day."

78
00:07:12.469 --> 00:07:16.022
And with that, the judge dismissed them from his court.

79
00:07:16.023 --> 00:07:19.022
Mrs. Blurrie went home and celebrated with Harry.

80
00:07:19.023 --> 00:07:29.330
Though she didn't have her valuables, she did have what was most valuable to her―the ability to see.

